From: OpenDesk <opendesk@openharmony.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 13:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] Lib/site.py: load HarmonyOS compatibility layer

Auto-import _harmonyos_compat module at Python startup to transparently
wrap subprocess calls with pipe syntax, working around SELinux domain
transition restrictions on HarmonyOS.

Files modified:
  Lib/site.py
---
diff --git a/Lib/site.py b/Lib/site.py
--- a/Lib/site.py
+++ b/Lib/site.py
@@ -557,6 +557,18 @@ def main():
     """
     global ENABLE_USER_SITE
 
+    # HarmonyOS compatibility layer - must be applied first
+    # This patches subprocess calls to work around SELinux restrictions
+    try:
+        import _harmonyos_compat
+        _harmonyos_compat.init()
+    except ImportError:
+        pass  # Module not available (non-HarmonyOS build)
+    except Exception as e:
+        # Don't let compat layer break Python startup
+        if os.environ.get('HARMONYOS_SUBPROCESS_DEBUG'):
+            print(f"[HarmonyOS-Compat] Error: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
+
     orig_path = sys.path[:]
     known_paths = removeduppaths()
     if orig_path != sys.path:
         # removeduppaths() might make sys.path absolute.
         # fix __file__ and __cached__ of already imported modules too.
         abs_paths()
